\title{rbe: Rule-Based Ensembles}
\description{
Fit RuleFit models for regression and classification, as described by Friedman and Popescu (2008) \doi{10.1214/07-AOAS148}. A boosted tree ensemble creates a set of rules, and a regularized generalized linear model from 'glmnet' is fit to the original predictors and binary indicators for the rules. The rules can be made with 'xgboost' (Chen and Guestrin (2016) \doi{10.1145/2939672.2939785}), 'lightgbm' (Ke et al. (2017) \url{https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2017/hash/6449f44a102fde848669bdd9eb6b76fa-Abstract.html}), or 'catboost' (Prokhorenkova et al. (2018) \doi{10.48550/arXiv.1706.09516}).
}
